node_modules/
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
.env
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# --- Android signing secrets: NEVER commit these ---
# The release keystore is the private key that identifies this app. Losing it
# means never being able to update a published app; leaking it lets someone
# else publish as you. Keep it outside this repo entirely.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pepk
keystore.properties
signing.properties
# Note: the '*' patterns above are not anchored, so they also match a keystore
# accidentally dropped into any subdirectory (e.g. android/app/release.jks).

# --- Android / Gradle build output ---
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.kotlin/
android/local.properties
android/captures/
android/.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
.idea/
*.iml

# --- graft (dev tooling only; nothing here reaches the server) ---
# graft/ is the code graph the Claude Code sessions query instead of reading
# source files. It is generated, not authored: ~14 MB of parse cache, wiring
# JSON and per-file cards, all derived from src/, android/, test/ and scripts/.
#
# It stays ignored even though sessions run on throwaway containers where an
# ignored directory does not survive. Committing it was the obvious fix and is
# the wrong one: a full rebuild takes about 4 seconds, needs no API key and
# costs nothing, while a committed graph would be a snapshot that silently rots
# — every commit that lands without regenerating it leaves the agent trusting
# file:line spans that have moved, which is worse than having no graph at all.
# It would also put a 14 MB generated blob in the history the VPS pulls.
#
# What makes it survive instead: .claude/helpers/graft-session-start.cjs, a
# SessionStart hook that rebuilds it when the container doesn't have one.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, unlike the keystore patterns above where the
# lack of one is deliberate. `graft init` writes this rule unanchored, and
# unanchored it also matches .claude/skills/graft/ — the instruction file that
# tells the agent the index exists — so the tool would quietly ignore the half
# of itself that has to be committed.
/graft/

# Fallback install prefix used by .claude/helpers/graft-ensure.cjs when the
# graft npm package cannot be installed globally. Machine-local, never shared.
.claude/.graft-runtime/

# Per-developer Claude Code overrides. .claude/settings.json is shared; this
# one is personal and would otherwise fight between machines.
.claude/settings.local.json
